            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>This Week's Observation: Tighter Account Audits, Three Suspension Types Dominate</h2>
<p>This week, 以渔数媒 received multiple requests for Google Ads account appeals, concentrated in three scenarios: landing pages flagged for 'Misleading Content', conversion tracking configurations triggering 'Circumvention' rules, and ad copy with sensitive industry terms being auto-blocked.</p>
<p>A typical case: A utility app team set their landing page CTA as 'Download Now', with subscription terms in fine print at the bottom. The system flagged this as 'Hidden Costs' and suspended the campaign. Appeal success rates for such issues hover around 60%, mainly because teams don't know which evidence materials to prepare.</p>
<p>Another notable change: Google's brand safety enforcement appears tighter this week. Several operations teams reported normal-running e-commerce creatives were taken down for using brand logos as decorative elements, triggering IP complaints. Appeal material requirements are longer than usual.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Appeal Material Checklist: Match Your Suspension Type</h2>
<p>Based on this week's cases, here's a type-specific material preparation guide:</p>
<p><strong>For 'Circumvention' suspensions, core materials include:</strong><br />
- Complete conversion tracking configuration screenshots (GA4, GTM, server-side events)<br />
- Technical architecture documentation of landing pages<br />
- Historical account performance data proving no artificial clicks or auto-refresh<br />
- If using third-party attribution tools, additional data flow diagrams required</p>
<p><strong>For 'Misleading Content' suspensions, prepare:</strong><br />
- Full-page screenshots or PDFs, especially pricing, terms, refund policies<br />
- Historical page version records (proving info wasn't recently added)<br />
- Comparison between product functionality and ad copy claims<br />
- For health/financial ads, supplementary qualification documents needed</p>
<p><strong>For 'Brand Safety/IP' suspensions, focus on:</strong><br />
- Copyright proof or authorization for used elements<br />
- Design source files proving legitimate usage<br />
- Clear explanation of intended use and context in appeal letter</p>
<hr />
<h2>One Detail That Makes or Breaks Your Appeal</h2>
<p>A common issue across this week's cases: complete materials prepared, but appeal letters too vague.</p>
<p>Review teams handle hundreds of appeals daily, spending under three minutes per case. Letters stating only 'Requesting unban due to system error' will likely be rejected outright.</p>
<p>Effective appeal letter structure:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Paragraph 1 (under 50 words):</strong> State specific suspension reason and account details<br />
<strong>Paragraph 2 (under 150 words):</strong> List corrective actions taken and materials prepared<br />
<strong>Paragraph 3 (under 100 words):</strong> Commit to future compliant advertising plans</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A positive example this week: A cross-border e-commerce team received 'Brand Safety' suspension, submitted complete copyright authorization, design source files, and a three-paragraph appeal letter within two hours. They received unban confirmation that afternoon—under six hours total.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Actionable Recommendations for Ad Teams</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Immediately audit all landing pages for compliance</strong>, especially pricing displays and terms text easily crawled by systems</li>
<li><strong>Prepare an appeal material kit in advance</strong>, including common screenshot templates and translated qualification documents in shared documents</li>
<li><strong>Appeal immediately upon suspension</strong>, never wait beyond 48 hours—faster response correlates with higher success rates this week</li>
<li><strong>Keep records of all configuration changes</strong>, review teams may request settings from specific time periods</li>
</ol>
<p>Contact us if you need help with account appeals—we provide case-specific diagnosis and material support.</p>
